      "body": "## Summary\n\n- use the native 64-bit HIP execution mask for the JIT QK-norm/RoPE kernel\n- mirror each logical-warp mask across both halves of a wave64\n- pass an explicit logical width of 32 to partial-RoPE shuffles\n- add focused gfx950 partial-NeoX correctness coverage\n\n## Motivation\n\nThe kernel is written around 32-lane logical warps, while HIP executes two of them in one wave64. A 32-bit mask and implicit shuffle width can select lanes from the other logical warp for partial-RoPE configurations.\n\nThis PR deliberately contains only the generic wave64 portability fix. The experimental MiMo DFLASH caller is excluded because it did not improve end-to-end throughput.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Python syntax and diff checks pass locally\n- focused gfx950 GPU test is included; full GPU CI is intentionally left to the draft review cycle\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41031013153](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41031013153)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41031013215](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41031013215)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41031012956](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41031012956)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
